★ INNOVATION DRIVES THE WORLD FORWARD ★
Mode that shapes economic behavior, cultural expectations, and secondary 
innovations. These attractors shift from electromechanical → digital → 
networked → intelligent → quantum‑adjacent.

Decade-by-decade 
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1960s — Electromechanical Massification
---------------------------------------
Dominant mode: broadcast + industrial miniaturization

Television — mass broadcast → shared cultural substrate
Transistor — miniaturization → portable electronics
Commercial_air_travel — global mobility → shrinking world
Microwave_oven — domestic automation
Space_exploration — geopolitical prestige + systems engineering

Structural invariant: energy → signal → mobility.

1970s — Personalization of Technology
---------------------------------------
Dominant mode: individual access to computation + media

Personal_computer — computation becomes personal
VCR — time‑shifting media
(Late‑70s seeds for mobile telephony)

Invariant: computation collapses from institutional → personal.

1980s — Digital Consumerization
---------------------------------------
Dominant mode: portable communication + digital media

Mobile_phone — mobility of communication
CD_player — digital audio → perfect reproduction
Invariant: digitization of signal.

1990s — Network Formation
---------------------------------------
Dominant mode: global connectivity

Email — asynchronous digital communication
GPS — global positioning → spatial computation
World_Wide_Web — hypertext + global information substrate

Invariant: addressability of people, places, and information.

2000s — Ubiquitous Digital Life
---------------------------------------
Dominant mode: always‑on digital presence

Digital_camera — visual capture becomes universal
Social_media — identity + social graph
Wi-Fi — wireless access → mobility of the internet

Invariant: continuous digital self.

2010s — Mobile Cloud Intelligence
---------------------------------------
Dominant mode: smart devices + cloud substrate

Smartphone — the meta‑device
Cloud_computing — elastic compute
Tablet — touch‑first computing
Artificial_intelligence — statistical learning at scale
Electric_vehicles — electrification + autonomy seeds

Invariant: compute becomes ambient.

2020s — Hyperconnected Autonomy
---------------------------------------
Dominant mode: real‑time sensing + generative intelligence

5G — low‑latency bandwidth → real‑time systems
Wearables — continuous physiological sensing
Drones — autonomous mobility
Generative_AI — synthetic cognition
Quantum_computing — non‑classical computation frontier

Invariant: autonomy + synthetic cognition.
